{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB09096 - MONDO_6554",
  "verbalization": "Benzoyl Peroxide is implicated in the development of Granuloma Annulare through a chain of indications that ultimately target the skin condition. The evidence suggests that Benzoyl Peroxide may be associated with Contact Dermatitis, which in turn is linked to Ammonium Lactate or Desoximetasone, both of which are indicated to cause Granuloma Annulare. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism where Benzoyl Peroxide could contribute to skin inflammation, leading to the formation of Granuloma Annulare. The overlapping indications across different pathways suggest a possible role of Benzoyl Peroxide in triggering inflammatory responses that result in the development of the condition. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader pharmacological context in assessing the potential reutilization of Benzoyl Peroxide for treating Granuloma Annulare.",
